Question

Compare subject marks in two examinations, identify improvements and declines, and flag subjects with low marks.

Algorithm

Read subjects and both mark lists.

Confirm the lists have matching lengths.

Compare marks for each subject.

Count subjects below the pass threshold and report the overall support status.

Flowchart

Start -> Input subjects and two mark lists -> Counts match? -> Compare each subject -> Mark below 40? -> Report trends and status -> End

Python Code

def performance_trend():

    subjects = input("Subject names separated by commas: ").split(",")

    first = [float(x) for x in input("First exam marks in same order: ").split()]

    second = [float(x) for x in input("Second exam marks in same order: ").split()]

    if len(subjects) != len(first) or len(first) != len(second):

        print("Enter one mark per subject for both exams.")

        return

    weak_count = 0

    for i in range(len(subjects)):

        change = second[i] - first[i]

        if change > 0:

            trend = "improved"

        elif change < 0:

            trend = "declined"

        else:

            trend = "unchanged"

        print(f"{subjects[i].strip()}: {trend} by {abs(change):.1f} marks")

        if second[i] < 40:

            weak_count += 1

    print("Overall result:", "Needs support" if weak_count else "No weak subjects")

 

performance_trend()

